# Keycloak tokens (they expire in 5 minutes). Copy the access_token of the response into the
# token variable of the file you are going to use:
#   @customerToken -> customer with a COMPLETE registration (role CUSTOMER_BASIC)
#   @registerToken -> customer halfway through registration (registration_status != COMPLETE)
#   @adminToken    -> admin-user (role ADMIN)
#   @serviceToken  -> transaction-service (role SERVICE), to call account-service directly
@keycloak = http://localhost:9090/realms/bank/protocol/openid-connect/token
@email = ana.martinez92@gmail.com
@password = secure1!

### Customer token (also the @registerToken during registration)
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=kong&client_secret=kong-client-secret&username={{email}}&password={{password}}

### Admin token
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=kong&client_secret=kong-client-secret&username=admin@bank.com&password=admin123

### transaction-service service token (client credentials)
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=transaction-service&client_secret=transaction-service-secret
